From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:21:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] block: restart instead of failing a sysfs store on a busy tag
 set lock

elv_iosched_store() and queue_requests_store() take the tag set's
update_nr_hwq_lock with down_write_trylock() and fail with -EBUSY when it
is not free. The trylock avoids a deadlock with del_gendisk(), which
holds the lock while kobject_del() waits for the active kernfs
references of the queue attributes. But the lock belongs to the tag set,
not to the disk: it is also held while any other disk of the same tag
set changes its scheduler or nr_requests, or while one is added. All
LUNs of one SCSI host share one tag set, so when udev sets the
scheduler of every disk at boot, each disk in its own worker, the
writes race and some of them fail at random:

  Failed to write "bfq" to sysfs attribute "queue/scheduler":
  Device or resource busy

On a UFS device with six LUNs four or five of them were left without
the configured scheduler at every boot.

Handle this as lock_device_hotplug_sysfs() handles the same problem for
the device hotplug lock: when the trylock fails, sleep briefly and
restart the system call. The restart drops the active reference, so a
concurrent del_gendisk() still completes (and the restarted write then
fails as the attribute is gone), while a write that only raced with a
sibling disk now waits for it and succeeds.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 block/blk-sysfs.c | 41 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 block/blk.h       |  1 +
 block/elevator.c  | 12 +++++++-----
 3 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/block/blk-sysfs.c b/block/blk-sysfs.c
index 520972676ab4..a317fa2e3045 100644
--- a/block/blk-sysfs.c
+++ b/block/blk-sysfs.c
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 #include <linux/backing-dev.h>
 #include <linux/blktrace_api.h>
 #include <linux/debugfs.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/sched/signal.h>
 
 #include "blk.h"
 #include "blk-mq.h"
@@ -62,6 +64,34 @@ static ssize_t queue_requests_show(struct gendisk *disk, char *page)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/**
+ * blk_sysfs_lock_update_nr_hwq - write-lock a tag set from a queue sysfs store
+ * @set: tag set of the queue whose attribute is being written
+ *
+ * A sysfs ->store() runs with an active reference on its kernfs node, and
+ * del_gendisk() waits for those references (kobject_del()) while it holds
+ * @set->update_nr_hwq_lock, so a store must not sleep on that lock.  A plain
+ * trylock however fails whenever any other disk of the same tag set holds the
+ * lock, e.g. when udev sets the I/O scheduler of all LUNs of one SCSI host at
+ * the same time, and the write then fails with -EBUSY for no real reason.
+ *
+ * Do what lock_device_hotplug_sysfs() does for the same problem: if the lock
+ * is not free, sleep briefly and restart the system call.  The restart drops
+ * the active reference, so a concurrent del_gendisk() can still finish, and
+ * the restarted write then fails because the attribute is gone.
+ *
+ * Return: 0 with the lock held for writing, or -ERESTARTNOINTR.
+ */
+int blk_sysfs_lock_update_nr_hwq(struct blk_mq_tag_set *set)
+{
+	if (down_write_trylock(&set->update_nr_hwq_lock))
+		return 0;
+
+	/* Avoid busy looping: 5 ms of sleep should do. */
+	fsleep(5 * USEC_PER_MSEC);
+	return restart_syscall();
+}
+
 static ssize_t
 queue_requests_store(struct gendisk *disk, const char *page, size_t count)
 {
@@ -70,7 +100,7 @@ queue_requests_store(struct gendisk *disk, const char *page, size_t count)
 	struct elevator_tags *et = NULL;
 	unsigned int memflags;
 	unsigned long nr;
-	int ret;
+	int ret, err;
 
 	ret = queue_var_store(&nr, page, count);
 	if (ret < 0)
@@ -80,13 +110,14 @@ queue_requests_store(struct gendisk *disk, const char *page, size_t count)
 	 * Serialize updating nr_requests with concurrent queue_requests_store()
 	 * and switching elevator.
 	 *
-	 * Use trylock to avoid circular lock dependency with kernfs active
-	 * reference during concurrent disk deletion:
+	 * Don't sleep on the lock, to avoid a circular lock dependency with the
+	 * kernfs active reference during concurrent disk deletion:
 	 *   update_nr_hwq_lock -> kn->active (via del_gendisk -> kobject_del)
 	 *   kn->active -> update_nr_hwq_lock (via this sysfs write path)
 	 */
-	if (!down_write_trylock(&set->update_nr_hwq_lock))
-		return -EBUSY;
+	err = blk_sysfs_lock_update_nr_hwq(set);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
 
 	if (nr == q->nr_requests)
 		goto unlock;
diff --git a/block/blk.h b/block/blk.h
index 2cc03aa54c53..5bd2814990f5 100644
--- a/block/blk.h
+++ b/block/blk.h
@@ -362,6 +362,7 @@ void elv_update_nr_hw_queues(struct request_queue *q,
 		struct elv_change_ctx *ctx);
 void elevator_set_default(struct request_queue *q);
 void elevator_set_none(struct request_queue *q);
+int blk_sysfs_lock_update_nr_hwq(struct blk_mq_tag_set *set);
 
 ssize_t part_size_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
 		char *buf);
diff --git a/block/elevator.c b/block/elevator.c
index 2161b6eea680..fbfd3f969c99 100644
--- a/block/elevator.c
+++ b/block/elevator.c
@@ -808,20 +808,22 @@ ssize_t elv_iosched_store(struct gendisk *disk, const char *buf,
 	ctx.type = elevator_find_get(ctx.name);
 
 	/*
-	 * Use trylock to avoid circular lock dependency with kernfs active
-	 * reference during concurrent disk deletion:
+	 * Don't sleep on update_nr_hwq_lock, to avoid a circular lock
+	 * dependency with the kernfs active reference during concurrent disk
+	 * deletion:
 	 *   update_nr_hwq_lock -> kn->active (via del_gendisk -> kobject_del)
 	 *   kn->active -> update_nr_hwq_lock (via this sysfs write path)
+	 * blk_sysfs_lock_update_nr_hwq() restarts the write instead of failing
+	 * it while another disk of the same tag set holds the lock.
 	 *
 	 * Use the writer lock instead of the reader lock of update_nr_hwq_lock
 	 * to serialize the two-stage elevator switch steps in
 	 * elevator_change(): the core switch step under the elevator lock and
 	 * the elevator_change_done() step outside the elevator lock.
 	 */
-	if (!down_write_trylock(&set->update_nr_hwq_lock)) {
-		ret = -EBUSY;
+	ret = blk_sysfs_lock_update_nr_hwq(set);
+	if (ret)
 		goto out;
-	}
 	if (!blk_queue_no_elv_switch(q)) {
 		ret = elevator_change(q, &ctx);
 		if (!ret)
